2026-10-29  Thalena Gundersen  <thalena1234@gmail.com>

	Annual warm-day frequency analysis in Uppsala for 1722-2022

	* Developed macros/WarmDays.C, a C++ ROOT macro analysing the annual frequency of warm days (urban-corrected mean temperature of at least 20C) in Uppsala between 1722 and 2022. 
	* The macro calculates annual warm-day frequencies as percentages, excludes years with fewer than 330 observations, and computes a trailing 30-year moving average requiring at least 27 valid years per window. It generates a combined graph exported in PNG and PDF formats. 

2026-10-29  Thalena Gundersen  <thalena1234@gmail.com>

	Uppsala preprocessing compatibility improvements

	* Following discussion with team members, revised the Uppsala preprocessing section to generate two separate output files:
		* data/cleaned/uppsala_tm_1722-2022.dat: unfiltered observations, retained for compatibility with another team member's analysis.
		* data/cleaned/filtered_uppsala_tm_1722-2022.dat: observations originating exclusively from Uppsala (source_id == 1).
	* The preprocessing removes Windows carriage-return characters and reports observation counts and potentially out-of-range temperatures for both datasets.

2026-10-28  Thalena Gundersen  <thalena1234@gmail.com>

	Uppsala source filtering  

	* Extended scripts/clean_data.sh to generate a filtered version of the historical Uppsala temperature dataset. The filtering procedure selects observations with source_id == 1 (column 6), corresponding to measurements originating from Uppsala. 
	* The filtered dataset was introduced to support analyses restricted to observations from Uppsala, rather than including measurements originating from other locations.

